From: patched-fork-bot <patched-fork-bot@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 1 Jan 2024 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] secure_tcp: no-op, self-hosted rendezvous servers never
 answer this handshake

secure_tcp() waits for the rendezvous/relay server to participate in a
key-exchange handshake that is only implemented server-side in RustDesk's
paid Server Pro product. Third-party self-hosted stacks (e.g.
lejianwen/rustdesk-server + lejianwen/rustdesk-api) never respond to it, so
every call site that reaches secure_tcp() (peer connections gated on
`key && (token || switch_code)`, plus the unconditional health-check and
rendezvous-mediator connections) hangs until READ_TIMEOUT and fails with
"Failed to secure tcp: deadline has elapsed: Please try later".

Connections without this handshake are already encrypted (see the
use_ws()/key-exchange path in secure_tcp_impl), so skipping it here is safe.

See: https://github.com/lejianwen/rustdesk-api/issues/92
     https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk/issues/13466
     https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk/commit/22eb19faa2693c4745777e99d2b1a2c87ddf1ca9

Upstream context drifts release to release — if this fails to apply, find
`pub async fn secure_tcp` in src/common.rs and re-diff by hand; do not skip.
---
 src/common.rs | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/src/common.rs b/src/common.rs
index 0000000..0000000 100644
--- a/src/common.rs
+++ b/src/common.rs
@@ -2043,5 +2043,6 @@
 }
 
 pub async fn secure_tcp(conn: &mut Stream, key: &str) -> ResultType<()> {
+    return Ok(());
     secure_tcp_impl(conn, key, true).await
 }
